      "selected_set": "electric-arc-37342FFF-v1",
      "retained_limits": [
        "Deterministic, no AI: the arcs are a stylised discharge (white zigzag core, blue sheath, dark-blue additive halo) drawn along the native centrelines, not photographed lightning. The zigzag is a smooth noise warp of +-0.25 texel, so it stays inside the native footprint and changes only where the native frame changes.",
        "Opaque (class 127) blue sheath fills the native opaque footprint exactly like the PSX; it reads as a tube in places where the native footprint is 3 texels wide.",
        "The arc frames also exist in CAFC4AA7 (brown/white) and the flash cell in 7B0E84A2, but the logs show 7B0E84A2 only on the arc frames and CAFC4AA7 only on the flash cell.",
        "Review composites and motion are SIMULATIONS (dark background, PSX semi-1 rule, bilinear RGB / nearest A, no mips); the live look (robin-0030/0120) still shows stock pixels. A live A/B is required.",
        "The other texels of the page (debris row, fire puffs, flash wedges) are never drawn in the logs and stay native."
      ],
